Getting Started & Controls Desktop Mode: Move using standard WASD keys, adjust your view with the mouse, and use the spacebar to jump. Navigating MenusQuick Menu & Main Menu: Access your profile, adjust audio settings, manage friends, and change avatars on the fly.Action Menu: Use radial gestures to trigger expressions, handle tools, or open the in-game Chatbox by navigating to Tools > Chatbox.Wings: Use the customizable widget menus attached to your main/quick menus for instant access to favorite content. [1] (<nowiki>https://wiki.vrchat.com/wiki/Chatbox</nowiki>), [2] ([[Main Menu|https://wiki.vrchat.com/wiki/Main_Menu]])VR & Hand Tracking: Use controllers for natural hand movements, or enable hand tracking on supported standalone headsets (like Meta Quest) to use pinch gestures for menus and movement. [1] (<nowiki>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oopovk3BPaw)Safety</nowiki> Mode: Press the designated safe mode key (or toggle via menu) to block unverified custom shaders or audio from unfamiliar users if your client lags or feels unsafe. [1] (<nowiki>https://wiki.vrchat.com/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Controls</nowiki>)